## JSON Manifest for db-agent

```json
{
  "target_agent": "db-agent",
  "context_files": [
    "prisma/schema.prisma",
    "components/shared/uerk.jsx",
    "components/shared/uerm.jsx",
    "components/shared/uerv.jsx"
  ],
  "task_description": "Add two new Prisma models to prisma/schema.prisma: LandingPage and LandingBlock, with enums LandingStatus and BlockType. LandingPage has fields: id (autoincrement), slug (unique String), title (String), titleSeo (optional String), descriptionSeo (optional Text), ogImageUrl (optional String), jsonLdType (optional String, default 'Product'), categoryId (optional Int, relation to Category with onDelete SetNull), status (LandingStatus enum, default DRAFT), blocks (LandingBlock[]), timestamps. LandingBlock has fields: id (autoincrement), landingPageId (Int, relation to LandingPage with onDelete Cascade), type (BlockType enum), content (Json), sortOrder (Int, default 0), visibility (Boolean, default true), timestamps. Add @@index([slug, status]) on LandingPage and @@index([landingPageId, sortOrder]) on LandingBlock. Map tables as 'landingpage' and 'landingblock'. LandingStatus enum: DRAFT, PUBLISHED, ARCHIVED. BlockType enum: HERO, PURPOSE, CONSTRUCTION, MODULES, TECH_SPECS, ADVANTAGES, COMPLETENESS, INSTALLATION, RELATED_PRODUCTS, CTA, FAQ, GALLERY, RICH_TEXT. Add the Category relation field 'landingPages LandingPage[]' to the existing Category model. Do NOT modify any existing model fields or indexes. Run 'npx prisma migrate dev --name add-landing-cms' after schema update.",
  "expected_output": "Updated prisma/schema.prisma with LandingPage, LandingBlock models, LandingStatus and BlockType enums, and a successful migration in prisma/migrations/. The existing schema remains byte-identical except for the new relation field on Category."
}
```

